==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{term/t|ang|hlāf||bread}} + a second element representing {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*daigijǭ||kneader}} (compare Old English [[dǣġe]], Old English {{term/t|ang|dāg}} "dough"). Similar to a [[kenning]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhlæːvdiːje/|[ˈɬæːvdiːjə]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hlǣfdīġe|f|hlǣfdīgan}}

# a [[lady]], the mistress of a household.